- qwen3-rerank-hybrid: qwen3-rerank (hybrid) reranking.
- qwen3-rerank: qwen3-rerank reranking.
- gte-rerank-hybrid: gte-rerank (hybrid) reranking.
- gte-rerank: gte-rerank reranking.



<props="intl">

- gte-rerank-hybrid: Official reranking.
- gte-rerank: gte-rerank reranking.






Default value: null. The reranking model selected when the knowledge base was created is used.


<props="china">

> If you only need semantic reranking, use qwen3-rerank. If you need both semantic reranking and text matching features to ensure relevance, use qwen3-rerank-hybrid.
>






<props="intl">

> If you only need semantic reranking, use gte-rerank. If you need both semantic reranking and text matching features to ensure relevance, use gte-rerank-hybrid.
>






<props="china">

> gte-rerank-hybrid and gte-rerank will no longer be updated and are not recommended.
>', example='gte-rerank-hybrid'),
      rerankInstruct?: string(name='RerankInstruct', description='<props="intl">This parameter is not available. Do not specify this parameter.

<props="china">A natural language instruction used to fine-tune the behavior of the reranking model.
<notice>This parameter takes effect only when rerank_mode is set to custom.</notice>', example='Given a web search query, retrieve relevant passages that answer the query.'),
      rerankMode?: string(name='RerankMode', description='<props="china">
The instruction intervention mode of the reranking model, which determines its scoring preference.

**Valid values:**

- **qa**: (Default) Q&A mode. The model tends to assign higher scores to candidates that can directly answer the query. Recommended for Q&A scenarios.

- **similar**: Similarity mode. The model tends to assign higher scores to candidates that are highly consistent with the query content. Recommended for matching and retrieval scenarios.

- **custom**: Custom mode. The reranking behavior of the model is determined by the instruction in the rerank_instruct parameter.



<props="intl">This parameter is not available. Do not specify this parameter.', example='qa'),
    }
  ](name='Rerank', description='The reranking configuration.', shrink='json', position='Query'),
  rerankMinScore?: float(name='RerankMinScore', description='The similarity threshold. This threshold specifies the minimum similarity score allowed for recalled text chunks and is used to filter the text chunks returned by the ranking model. Only text chunks with a score greater than this value are recalled. Valid values: 0.01 to 1.00. This parameter has a higher priority than the similarity threshold configured for the knowledge base.

If no specific value is specified, the similarity threshold configured for the knowledge base is used by default.', example='0.20', position='Query'),
  rerankTopN?: int32(name='RerankTopN', description='The top N text chunks to return after reranking. Valid values: 1 to 20. Default value: 5.', example='5', position='Query'),
  rewrite?: [ 
    {
      modelName?: string(name='ModelName', description='The name of the multi-turn conversation rewriting model. The model automatically adjusts the original input prompt (user question) based on the conversation context to improve retrieval performance. Valid values:
